  - The Horror Factor save is "+1 at levels 1, 2, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13 and 15", stored as a level-one bonus plus eight at_level steps. "+1 additional attack per melee round" is a flat combat bonus.
  - The natural A.R. of 6 and the +5% Espionage/Wilderness bonus are prose: the app has no natural armor field and no race-level per-skill modifier.
  - The "R.C.C. Skills" line is granted as occ_skills; Wolfen has no language row, so it is `Language: Other`. The extra Ancient W.P. is the same choice list as `rifts-wolfen`.
  - occ_restrictions is read from the "O.C.C.s Rifts" line. It says "technically any O.C.C." and then rules out the Operator, power armor pilots, and any cybernetic, bionic or other unnatural augmentation - so the except list names the Operator, the power armor and Glitter Boy pilots, and every full conversion ''Borg, Crazy and Juicer O.C.C. the catalog holds. "Most avoid" robot and vehicle skills is a tendency, not a bar, so robot pilots are not excepted. An O.C.C. of any named kind imported later is allowed until it is added.
  - Psionics: "Standard, basically same as humans", so no psionics block.
  - The section-wide rule on printed 74 - a new arrival from the Palladium World picks up the regional language and two Modern W.P.s within weeks, then three Rifts skills from Communications, Pilot (basic vehicles), Technical and W.P. Modern after 2D4+4 months or one level, and one more language or skill every two levels - applies to a character who came from Palladium rather than one raised on Rifts Earth. It is not stored; the survey carries it.
